message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The maximum Laplacian ratio of a tree: a complete answer to a question of Brualdi and Goldwasser, kernel-checked in Lean"
authors:
  - family-names: Murphy
    given-names: Peter W.
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/brualdi-goldwasser"
url: "https://drmurphyisin.github.io/brualdi-goldwasser/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: v1.4.2
date-released: 2026-10-07
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23046040
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23046040
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v1.2.0"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22983412
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI (all versions; resolves to the latest)"
keywords:
  - Laplacian permanent
  - Laplacian ratio
  - trees
  - extremal graph theory
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Brualdi-Goldwasser
abstract: >-
  For every n >= 4, the tree on n vertices maximizing per L(T) / prod deg(v) is an explicit spider of
  cherry arms; the maximum grows exactly like ((621/64)^(1/11))^n. The proof is formalized in Lean 4
  with Mathlib and checked by the Lean kernel.
